VeridianOS: port KirigamiApp to KLocalizedQmlContext and TreeViewPlugin off baseUrl()

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build (KF 6.30, Qt 6.12):

- src/app/kirigamiapp.cpp:33, :35: 'KLocalizedContext' is deprecated: Since
  6.8. use KLocalizedQmlContext or KLocalization::setupLocalizedContext()
  from KF6::I18nQml instead [-Wdeprecated-declarations].
  KirigamiApp::start() now installs a KLocalizedQmlContext, set up exactly
  as KLocalization::setupLocalizedContext() does (setContextObject() +
  QQmlEngine::setContextForObject()), but without applying this library's
  own TRANSLATION_DOMAIN ("kirigami_app6"), which the inline helper would
  set and which must not become the application's QML domain; the old code
  set no domain either. A context object the application installed itself
  is kept as before: a KLocalizedQmlContext, or the deprecated
  KLocalizedContext (matched with QObject::inherits() so the deprecated type
  is not named). Previously an application-installed KLocalizedQmlContext
  was replaced. KirigamiApp now links KF6::I18nQml (exported by the same
  KF6I18n package it already finds). KLocalizedQmlContext also re-evaluates
  the application's QML translations when the application language changes
  at runtime, marks i18n bindings as translation bindings, and makes the
  KI18n QML singleton available; KLocalizedContext did none of these.
- src/treeview/treeviewplugin.h:24, :28: 'QQmlExtensionPlugin::baseUrl()' is
  deprecated: Provide a qmldir file to remove the need for calling baseUrl
  [-Wdeprecated-declarations]. The module has a generated qmldir with
  "prefer :/qt/qml/org/kde/kirigamiaddons/treeview/", and
  ecm_target_qml_sources() compiles TreeViewDecoration.qml and
  styles/org.kde.desktop/TreeViewDecoration.qml into the plugin under that
  resource prefix. resolveFilePath()/resolveFileUrl() now use that prefix
  instead of the installed directory reported by baseUrl(). The style
  selection logic is unchanged; the selected component is loaded from the
  plugin's embedded copy (the copy the qmldir already tells the engine to
  prefer, built from the same source file) rather than the loose installed
  file. One case differs: when the module was resolved through its qrc
  qmldir (the prefer path; the plugin already loaded, or linked
  statically), baseUrl() was a qrc: URL whose toLocalFile() is empty, so
  no style directory was ever found and the unstyled file was used; the
  resource path finds the style in that case too. (0002 warns if the
  prefix ever stops matching.)

